# M1055: keep the docker build context honest.
#
# Every module Dockerfile COPYs the whole services/ reactor then builds it again inside the
# image — by design (the reactor needs the parent pom and the sibling poms). Without this
# file, the context also carries the already-built fat jars and class files from a previous
# host-side mvn run, making docker build slower and the temporary image fatter for no reason.
# The reactor itself rebuilds inside the container; nothing of the host's target/ is needed.

target/
*.class
.idea/
.vscode/
.classpath
.project
.settings/
out/

# The build context reaches this directory's root: never ship the host's own notes or scratch.
*.log
*.tmp
scratch-*
